  "id": "catastrophe-theory",
  "term": "catastrophe theory",
  "definition": "Catastrophe theory is an approach for describing how a system can shift abruptly from a stable state to an unstable one when ongoing change reaches a critical point. In the packet, it is used in cusp form to track stability with an indicator that changes sign as the system crosses that threshold.",
